# Only generated / gitignored paths are excluded — never a tracked file.
#
# Two reasons this list is what it is (#225):
#  - The builder reads the commit from `.git` via Go's -buildvcs so a source build
#    reports its version. `.git` is therefore kept IN the context (it reaches the
#    builder stage only; the runtime stage copies just the binary).
#  - -buildvcs also records whether the built tree was modified. Dropping a TRACKED
#    file here would make git see a deletion and stamp a clean checkout as "-dirty",
#    so tracked files (docs, .github, *.md, the compose file, this file) stay in.
#    The entries below are all gitignored, so excluding them changes nothing git sees
#    — they are just build artifacts the Go binary does not need, and leaving
#    node_modules out keeps the context small.
web/node_modules
web/build
web/.svelte-kit
/yaadegar
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
*.db-journal
